                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            This entry is concerned with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi VectBund
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are allowed to cover non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
            between their base spaces.
          %p
            This means that after choosing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            and an ambient category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            (e.g.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TopologicalSpaces"} TopologicalSpaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothManifolds"} SmoothManifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi VectBund
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
                over any base space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                in the ambient category, which we shall denote like this:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo [
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi E
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi B
                        %mo ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left[
                      \\array{
                      E
                      \\\
                      \\big\downarrow
                      \\\
                      B
                      }
                      \\right]
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi VectBund
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+squares"} commuting squares
                (in the ambient category of spaces) of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi E
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi ϕ
                            %mtd
                              %mi E
                              %mo ′
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                              %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      E &amp;\overset{\phi}{\longrightarrow}&amp; E'
                      \\\
                      \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                      \\\
                      B &amp;\underset{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B'
                      }
              %p
                which are
                = succeed "-wise" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
              %p
                Notice here that given the base map
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                into the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+vector+bundle"} pullback vector bundle
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mi E
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast E'
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi E
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi ϕ
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi f
                                %mo *
                              %mi E
                              %mo ′
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↙
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      E &amp;&amp; \overset{\phi}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; f^\ast E'
                      \\\
                      \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; B
                      }
          %p
            Accordingly, for each base space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            there is a
            = succeed "-inclusion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi VectBund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                  %mi VectBund
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  VectBund(B)
                  \\xhookrightarrow{\phantom{--}}
                  VectBund
          %p
            of the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/VectBund%28X%29"} VectBund(B)
            of vector bundles over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#BireflectiveInclusionOfZeroBundles Bireflective inclusion of zero-bundles
          %p
            The construction which to any base space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            assigns the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-vector+bundle"} zero-vector bundle
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            constitutes a
            = succeed "-inclusion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bireflective+subcategory"} bireflective subcategory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "bireflective+subcategory#ZeroVectorBundlesAmongVectorBundles"} there
          %h3#ClosedMonoidalStructures Closed monoidal structures
          %p
            For a fixed base space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures"} structures
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/VectBund%28B%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi VectBund
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund_B
            are well known, given
            = succeed "-wise" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/VectorSpaces"} VectorSpaces
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+structure"} cartesian monoidal structure
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi VectBund
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund(B)
                is given by
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
                = succeed "-wise" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %li
              %p
                the other
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+structure"} symmetric monoidal structure
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi VectBund
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund(B)
                is given by
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+bundles"} tensor product of vector bundles
                = succeed "-wise" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
          %p
            But analogous – if subtly different – monoidal structures exist on the total category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi VectBund
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#TensorMonoidalStructur"} Cartesian monoidal structure on VectBund
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#TensorMonoidalStructur"}> Tensor monoidal structure on VectBund
                \.
          %p
            In discussing this now, we (have to and want to) assume that the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TopologicalSpaces"} TopologicalSpaces
            is itself
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            (a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"}> convenient category of topological spaces
            ”), such as that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
            or of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topological+spaces"} D-topological spaces
          %h4#CartesianMonoidalStructure Cartesian monoidal structure
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
