            We want to point out a way in which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi VectBund
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund
            with its
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/external+tensor+product"} external tensor product
          %ol
            %li
              %p vector spaces equipped with their tensor product,
            %li
              %p vector spaces equipped with parametrization, namely vector bundles,
          %p at least in the case that the base space is discrete.
          %p
            The argument generalizes immediately to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+vector+bundles"} flat vector bundles
            over arbitrary base spaces (by enhancing the following parameter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            to
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoids"} fundamental groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-vector+bundle"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-vector bundles
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+infinity-connection"}
              flat
              = succeed "-connections" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            (by enhancing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoids"} fundamental groupoids
            further to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+infinity-groupoids"}
              fundamental
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+vector+spaces"} category of vector spaces
            to the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+chain+complexes"} (infinity,1)-category of chain complexes
          %p
            In order to formalize this idea, we need to work inside a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            which suitably subsumes all of the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/very+large+category"} very large
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-categories"} (2,1)-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi MonCat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MonCat
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CoCartCart
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CoCartCart
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocartesian+monoidal+categories"} cocartesian monoidal categories
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi DistMonCat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DistMonCat
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+monoidal+categories"} distributive monoidal categories
                (with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocartesian+monoidal+categories"} cocartesian monoidal categories
          %p Here we understand that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
                in these
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
                which respect all given
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
                up to
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functors"} strong monoidal functors
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
                between these functors.
          %p
            The system of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functors"} 2-functors
            between these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-categories"} (2,1)-categories
            forms a square
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            which we may regard as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of a corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"} contravariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            from the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram+category"} diagram category
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2Cat"} 2Cat
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
