                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi MonCat
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟵
                        %mtd
                          %mi DistMonCat
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Cat
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟵
                        %mtd
                          %mi CoCartCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{C}
                  \\;\;
                  \\colon
                  \\;\;
                  \\array{
                  (1,0) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; (1,1)
                  \\\
                  \\big\uparrow &amp;&amp; \big\uparrow
                  \\\
                  (0,0) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; (1,0)
                  }
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  \\mapsto
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  \\array{
                  MonCat &amp;\longleftarrow&amp; DistMonCat
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  Cat &amp;\longleftarrow&amp; CoCartCat
                  }
          %p
            The 2-categorical context which we are after is then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (2,1)-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \mathbf{C}
            on this
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
            are functors which strictly preserve the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
            present on their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            category, but whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            may be equipped with further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
            (though not with fewer tensor products).
          %p
            %strong Claim.
            In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \mathbf{C}
            the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            is a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"}> homotopy
            )
