            %p
              We need to see that this uniquely admits the dashed arrow. Unwinding the definitions, the existence of the dashed arrow means that any functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \,\colon\, Vect_{Set} \to \mathcal{C}
              which preserves both the coproduct of vector bundles as well as the tensor product on fibers already respects the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/external+tensor+product"} external tensor product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+monoidal+category"} distributivity
              and using that any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of its elements:
